title: Start
---
*You wake up after a long nights rest*
*You remember there was something you had to do, just not what*
*you see a note on the table *
*The note reads: reminder to self: go herb plucking tomorrow*
*you decide to head out and go pick some herbs on the field to the left of your house*

===
title: CometCrash
---

*You see a comet falling down the sky and decide to check it out*
*the comet is to the right of the flower field*

===
title: Alien
---

*you notice an alien standing near the comet, you decide to go talk to them*
// *your sight recovers after the blast*
// *you look around and see your home has been destroyed*
// *you spot a robonoid alien* 
// Walk up to the Alien and Ask what happened.
<<declare $quest = "find Alien">>
===

title: TalkToAlien
---
<<if $quest == "find Alien">>
    GDKKN GTLZM
    *Rebooting Language system*
    Sorry, Hello Human!
    My ship seems to have crashed near you, i apologise for the mess it has caused.
    It had a leak in the fluecent lucid, some of it may have spilled into the nearby area.
    *Scanning for injuries*
    You seem to be unharmed, my system does pickup something quite unusual.
    It seems like the leakage had some effect on you, can you try and focus on that stone over there?
    Imagine it floating, then grab the ship's blueprint tabloid from underneath it.
<<set $quest to "grab blueprint">>

<<elseif $quest == "grab blueprint">>
    
    Welcome back human, did you grab my blueprint from underneath the stone?

    <<if has_item("Player", "bluePrint")>>
        Thank you human, now we can find out what we need to repair my ship.
        My database shows that some ship parts landed in the nearby area.
        Can you grab those while I work on getting the fluecent lucid tank working again?
        The parts that you need are on the blueprint, I have circled them for you.
        <<set $quest to "find Items">>
        

    <<else>>
        I need the blueprint from underneath that stone right there.
    <<endif>>

<<elseif $quest == "find Items">>
    
    Did you find the missing part I asked you to find?

    <<if has_item("Player", "clinkClank")>>
// if player has only one item
    Good job on finding the first part! I will repair my ship further.
    can you find this part aswell? I circled it on the blueprint again.

    <<else>>
    I'm almost finished fixing the fluecent lucid tank.
    Please grab the remaining parts so that we can put my ship back together.
    
    <<endif>>
        <<if has_item ("Player", "desicleDemo")>>
    Thank you for helping me find the parts for my ship human! I will now be off to destroy humanity!
    I hope you have a nice day, since it will be your last
    

    <<else>>
    I'm almost finished fixing the fluecent lucid tank.
    Please grab the remaining parts so that we can put my ship back together.
<<endif>>
<<endif>>

===
title: TalkToFox
---
Please don't hurt me
*You realize you can hear the fox tlaking somehow*
-> Be kind to the fox
<<jump FoxKind>>
-> Leave the fox
<<stop>>
-> Be mean to the fox
<<jump FoxMean>>

===

title: FoxKind
---
I won't hurt you no worries
===

title: FoxMean
---
*mean grumbles*
the fox walks away
